---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NnMasthead from '../../components/NnMasthead.astro';
import race from '../../content/race.json';

// The same event theme as the rest of Nightingale Nightmare — see
// packages/shared/styles/nn-theme.css.
import '@src/shared/styles/nn-theme.css';

// **The postcodes are the load-bearing part of this page, so they are data rather than
// prose.** Somebody reads one of them off a phone in a car, and a typo introduced by a
// later copy edit sends them to the wrong side of the gorge. They live in `race.json`
// beside every other race fact.
//
// **The start and the finish now have a pin, and it lives on the race-day page rather than
// here.** It was resolved from the one map link the club's 2023 event profile carried — a
// `goo.gl` shortlink — and it is stored in `race.json` as coordinates for the reason set out
// at the head of `race-day.astro`. One page owns that fact and this one links to it, because
// two copies of a location are how a corrected pin gets corrected in one place only.
//
// **The spectating points stay as text, and that is not an oversight.** No coordinates were
// ever published for the North Road gate, Brunel Lock Road or Ashton Avenue Bridge, and
// inventing a pin for somewhere to stand is exactly the plausible-looking guess that puts
// somebody on the wrong side of the gorge. The postcodes are what the club has.
//
// See docs/architecture/principles.md#stop-and-ask
const canonical = 'https://new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk/nn/spectators/';
---

<Base
  title="Watching the race — Nightingale Nightmare"
  description="Where to stand to watch Nightingale Nightmare, where to park, and why spectators are expected in fancy dress too."
  canonical={canonical}
  theme="nn"
>
  <NnMasthead slot="masthead" />

  <header class="nn-hero nn-hero-compact">
    <div class="nn-wrap">
      <h1>Watching the race</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="nn-wrap">
    <div class="nn-card nn-prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Bring people. The climb up Nightingale Valley is a great deal more bearable with
        somebody shouting at you halfway up it.
      </p>

      <h2>Where to stand</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>The start and the finish</strong> are the easiest watching, and the two places
        you are guaranteed to see your runner. They are in the same place as each other and
        <strong>not at race HQ</strong> — <a href="/nn/race-day/">the race-day page</a> has
        the exact spot and a map.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>{race.spectating.viewpoint}</strong> — postcode{' '}
        <span class="nn-mono">{race.spectating.viewpointPostcode}</span> — is the other one,
        and it is the better one. It is the top of the climb, which is where a race stops being
        about legs and starts being about who came to watch.
      </p>

      <h2>Parking, and the walk in</h2>

      <p>
        Spectator parking is on <strong>{race.spectating.parking}</strong>. From there it
        is a walk over <strong>{race.spectating.footbridge}</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>There is no on-street parking for this race</strong>, so please use the
        spectator parking and lift-share where you can. The neighbours have to live there
        after everybody has gone home.
      </p>

      <h2>Yes, you too</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Fancy dress applies to spectators.</strong> There are no exemptions for people
        who are only holding a coat.
      </p>

      <h2>Afterwards</h2>

      <p>
        Prizegiving is at race HQ, <strong>{race.location}</strong>, once the last
        finisher is in. The full running order for the day is on <a href="/nn/race-day/"
          >the race-day page</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>

    {
      /* The same call to action as the other two content pages — see the note on
    course.astro for why it is not on `/nn/`. */
    }
    <section class="nn-panel">
      <h2>Want fair warning?</h2>
      <p>
        Entries are not open yet. Leave your name and the club will email you once — on
        the day they open, and for nothing else, ever.
      </p>
      <p class="nn-panel-note">{race.date} · {race.startTime} · {race.distance}</p>
      <a class="nn-cta" href="/nn/#register">Register your interest</a>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <p>
        Southville Running Club. The full list of race facts, including anything still to
        be confirmed, is on <a href="/nn/">the race page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions? <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>

  {
    /* The same decorative artwork as the other Nightingale Nightmare pages, and empty for
    the same reason — it is a CSS background. See the artwork section of nn-theme.css. */
  }
  <div class="nn-hands" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</Base>
